\ls83\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
That Intel UEFI is closer to normal PC firmware.\
\ls83\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
People 
\f4\i have
\f0\i0  dumped and patched it with external SPI programmers, but that\'92s full-on firmware hacking / risk of perma-bricking, and it still sits under T2 for newer machines.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf0 So on an old, non-T2 Intel Mac you can 
