\f7\b\fs40 \cf0 2. Biometric integration: where can GhostLink actually plug in?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs32 \cf0 Biometrics on Apple devices is 
\f3\b completely owned by the Secure Enclave
\f0\b0 :\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls103\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Sensor (Touch ID / Face ID / Optic ID) sends raw data over a 
\f3\b secure, dedicated link
\f0\b0  to the Secure Enclave, not to the main CPU.\
\ls103\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Secure Enclave processes, encrypts, and stores the biometric template.\
\ls103\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
During auth, it compares new input to stored template and returns only a 
\f3\b yes/no + maybe a key or token
\f0\b0 , never the raw biometric.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.apple.com/guide/security/biometric-security-sec067eb0c9e/web?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs18 \cf9 \cb10 CICS\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cf11 \cb10 +3\cf9 Apple Support\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cf11 \cb10 +3\cf9 Apple Support\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cf11 \cb10 +3}}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf0 So:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls104\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
There is no API to \'93sniff Touch ID frames\'94 or \'93inject into Face ID matching.\'94\
\ls104\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The enclave runs its own tiny secure OS and even has its own secure-boot chain. You don\'92t patch that either.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 What you 
\f11\i can
\f3\i0  do:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf0 On macOS / iOS, your code can talk to biometrics via 
\f3\b LocalAuthentication
\f0\b0  / Keychain APIs:{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/%40gauravharkhani01/app-security-in-swift-keychain-biometrics-secure-enclave-69359b4cffba?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs18 \cf9 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf9 \cb10 Medium\cb1 \
}}\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls105\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\'93Only unlock this key / perform this action if Face ID / Touch ID succeeds.\'94\
\ls105\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
You never see the fingerprint; you just get \'93auth succeeded, here\'92s the key\'94 or \'93nope.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf0 So for GhostLink, realistic biometric wiring looks like:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls106\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Personal vault / console unlock:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls106\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
GhostLink client or admin console requires Touch ID / Face ID to unlock its UI, config, or private key material.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls106\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Privileged actions:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls106\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\'93Reconfigure node,\'94 \'93wipe shard,\'94 \'93attach new hardware,\'94 etc. gated with biometric prompts.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls106\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Session binding:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls106\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Treat a successful biometric auth as \'93prove the human who owns this device is present,\'94 binding that to a session key GhostLink uses for that node.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf0 What you 
\f4\i cannot
\f0\i0  do is:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls107\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Replace system unlock with GhostLink.\
